# World Chronicle core and the continent line (world/chronicle.js, world/commands.js, design/data/world.toml; WP-W1 of
# design/architecture/world-state.md). Every `ttl world expect` / `ttl story expect` prints "ttl: ..." when it does not hold.
# `ttl world testmark` saves the real world and starts a blank one in which test bots count; `ttl world testrestore` at the
# end puts the real world back, so this run never moves the server's chronicle (milestones, balance, phases, firsts).
# `testthreshold 3 0` pins the milestone threshold at 3 souls whatever the active count is.
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] world: test mark set", "[ttl] world: milestone act2_reached reached", "[ttl] world: tide none -> dark",
# "[ttl] world: phase tempest village -> town (ops ...)", "... test mark set, the place's hook is skipped", "[ttl] world: test state restored".
# Verify in game (not asserted): `/ttl world where` on a boat ~200 blocks off the coast reads "outside"; the Voice line
# "Tempest has grown into a town ..." reaches each bot once; the title "Tempest grows".
ttl world testmark
ttl world testthreshold 3 0
ttl world expect test yes
ttl world expect threshold 3
ttl world expect counts.souls 0
ttl world expect milestone act2_reached no
# The continent line (R11): Tempest is inside, 9000 0 is beyond the map (open sea / free lands), the Labyrinth counts as
# inside, the Mortal Realm (Life 1) is never part of it.
ttl world expect continent 0 0 yes
ttl world expect continent 435 -1106 yes
ttl world expect continent 9000 0 no
ttl world expect continent 0 9000 no
ttl world expect continentin tensura:labyrinth 9000 0 yes
ttl world expect continentin ttl:spirit_domain 0 0 yes
ttl world expect continentin ttl:mortal_realm 0 0 no
# tensura:boss_area (Tensura's own Gazel/Hinata boss dimension) stays outside the story rules: owner decision, design/decisions.md 19/11/2026
ttl world expect continentin tensura:boss_area 0 0 no
ttl world at 0 0
ttl world at 9000 0
ttlbot spawn TtlBotWorldA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotWorldB
ttlbot spawn TtlBotWorldC
@sleep 2
ttl reset TtlBotWorldA
ttl reset TtlBotWorldB
ttl reset TtlBotWorldC
kubejs stages add TtlBotWorldA ttl.life2
kubejs stages add TtlBotWorldB ttl.life2
kubejs stages add TtlBotWorldC ttl.life2
ttl world forget TtlBotWorldA
ttl world forget TtlBotWorldB
ttl world forget TtlBotWorldC
# Three light Oaths (Act I comes with the Oath): souls and oaths are counted once per soul.
ttl story oath light TtlBotWorldA
ttl story oath light TtlBotWorldB
ttl story oath light TtlBotWorldC
ttl world expect counts.souls 3
ttl world expect counts.oaths.light 3
ttl world expect counts.acts.light.1 3
# Act II by two souls: below the threshold, nothing is written into the world yet.
ttl story act TtlBotWorldA 2
ttl story act TtlBotWorldB 2
ttl world expect counts.acts.light.2 2
ttl world expect milestone act2_reached no
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldA stage ttl.world.act2 no
# The third soul: the milestone is reached, sticky, and its stage is mirrored on every online Life 2 soul.
ttl story act TtlBotWorldC 2
ttl world expect counts.acts.light.2 3
ttl world expect counts.reached.2 3
ttl world expect milestone act2_reached yes
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldA stage ttl.world.act2 yes
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldC stage ttl.world.act2 yes
# A fourth soul gets the world's stages at login. A test bot comes back with fresh data after `ttlbot remove`/`spawn`
# (Life 1 again), so the login is the same call the PlayerEvents.loggedIn handler makes: `ttl world sync`.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotWorldD
@sleep 2
ttl reset TtlBotWorldD
kubejs stages add TtlBotWorldD ttl.life2
ttl world forget TtlBotWorldD
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldD stage ttl.world.act2 no
ttl world sync TtlBotWorldD
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldD stage ttl.world.act2 yes
ttl world expect counts.souls 4
# Balance and tide: -40 raises the dark tide (tide_at 25) with its unlocks, mood and stage; back to ~0 it ebbs.
ttl world balance add -40
ttl world expect tide dark
ttl world expect unlocked holy_hunt yes
ttl world expect mood tempest -1
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldB stage ttl.world.tide.dark yes
ttl world balance add 40
ttl world expect tide none
ttl world expect unlocked holy_hunt no
ttl world expect mood tempest 0
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldB stage ttl.world.tide.dark no
# A forced milestone: Tempest's phase rises to town (the grow hook is skipped under the test mark and logs it),
# its unlocks stay (sticky), its stage reaches every soul.
ttl world expect phase tempest village
ttl world milestone fire tempest_town
ttl world expect milestone tempest_town yes
ttl world expect phase tempest town
ttl world expect unlocked horde_raid yes
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldB stage ttl.world.phase.tempest.town yes
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldD stage ttl.world.phase.tempest.town yes
# A conflict opens and closes (exact mirror).
ttl world conflict open dwargon
ttl world expect conflict dwargon yes
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldA stage ttl.world.conflict.dwargon yes
ttl world conflict close dwargon
ttl world expect conflict dwargon no
ttl story expect TtlBotWorldA stage ttl.world.conflict.dwargon no
# A flag milestone with a mood (first Demon Lord: holy_church -1).
ttl story set TtlBotWorldD dark
ttl story flag TtlBotWorldD demon_lord
ttl world expect counts.flags.demon_lord 1
ttl world expect milestone first_demon_lord yes
ttl world expect mood holy_church -1
ttl world
ttl world log 6
ttl world export
# Put the real world back; the bots go.
ttl world testrestore
ttl world expect test no
ttlbot remove TtlBotWorldA
ttlbot remove TtlBotWorldB
ttlbot remove TtlBotWorldC
ttlbot remove TtlBotWorldD
